2370		$D_{|\ell}$ denote $D$ conditioned on the first element being $\ell$.
2371		For every line $\ell$ in $\F_q^{2m+2}$ and $f \in \deg_{md+1}(\ell)$
2372		define
2373		\[
2374			\hat{Q}^{\ell}_{f}
2375			= \E_{(\ell_X,\ell_Z) \sim D_{|\ell}}
2376			\sum_{\substack{f_X \in \deg_{md}(\ell_X),\
2377				f_Z \in \deg_{md}(\ell_Z):\\
2378				f = \mathrm{combine}_{f_X,f_Z}}}
2379			T^{\ell_X,\ell_Z}_{f_X,f_Z}\,,
2380		\]
2381		a valid POVM; the polynomial $\mathrm{combine}_{f_X,f_Z}$ of
2382		Definition~\ref{def:combine-map} is well defined here because Property~2
2383		of Lemma~\ref{lem:qld-sublines} guarantees that $\ell_X$ and $\ell_Z$
2384		are compatible with $\ell$. If $\ell$ is axis-parallel, then by
2385		Property~3 of Lemma~\ref{lem:qld-sublines} so are $\ell_X$ and
2386		$\ell_Z$, hence $f_X, f_Z \in \deg_d$ by Lemma~\ref{lem:qld-xz-lines};
2387		along such a line either $(\alpha,\beta)$ is constant, in which case
2388		$f = \mathrm{combine}_{f_X,f_Z}$ is a fixed linear combination of
2389		polynomials of degree at most $d$, or $(x,z)$ is constant, in which case
2390		$f$ is affine in the line parameter, so in either case
2391		$f \in \deg_d(\ell)$. Chaining Lemmas~\ref{lem:claim-17-1},
2392		\ref{lem:claim-17-2} and~\ref{lem:claim-17-3} with the triangle
2393		inequality for scalars gives the consistency bound
2394		\begin{equation}
2395			\label{eq:qld-combined-lines-consistency}
2396			\E_{(\ell,\ell_X,\ell_Z) \sim D}\
2397			\E_{(x,z,\alpha,\beta) \in \ell}
2398			\sum_{f_X,f_Z} \bra{\hat\psi}
2399			\big(T^{\ell_X,\ell_Z}_{f_X,f_Z}\big)_{\mathsf{A}\mathsf{A}'} \ot
2400			\big(\Id - \hat{Q}^{x,z}_{f_X(x),f_Z(z)}
2401			\big)_{\mathsf{B}\mathsf{A}''}
2402			\ket{\hat\psi}
2403			= O\big(m\,(\eps^{1/4} + \delta_P^{1/4} + \delta_Q^{1/4}
2404			+ \delta_{\mathrm{Line}}^{1/2})\big)\,;
2405		\end{equation}
2406		since
2407		$\delta_P = \poly(\eps, md/q)$, $\delta_Q = \poly(\eps)$, and
2408		$\delta_{\mathrm{Line}} = \poly(\eps)$, the right-hand side is a
2409		function of the form $m \cdot \poly(\eps, md/q)$. This established
2410		bound is not of the stated form $\poly(m^2\eps, md/q)$, and no
2411		function of that form dominates it, so the error function claimed in
2412		the statement remains unproved along this route; the source's second
2413		route rests on a joint-law decomposition not provided by Property~2 of
2414		Lemma~\ref{lem:qld-sublines}, and the established bound is the one
2415		used in the sequel (Remark~\ref{rem:qld-4-13-source-defects}; the two
2416		routes are analyzed in \cite{gap:qpbt_combined-lines-error-term}). Now
2417		if the pair $(f_X, f_Z)$ evaluates to $(a, b)$ at $(x, z)$, then
2418		$\mathrm{combine}_{f_X,f_Z}$ evaluates to $\alpha a + \beta b$ at
2419		$(x, z, \alpha, \beta)$; hence the consistency of $T$ with
2420		$\hat{Q}^{x,z}$ along the sub-line pairs expressed by
2421		\eqref{eq:qld-combined-lines-consistency}, the definition of
2422		$\hat{Q}^{\ell}$ as the image of $T$ under the combining map, and the
2423		construction of $\hat{Q}^{x,z,\alpha,\beta}$ in
2424		Lemma~\ref{lem:qld-4-12} as the corresponding coarse-graining of
2425		$\hat{Q}^{x,z}$ together yield the first relation of
2426		\eqref{eq:qld-4-13}, with the established error
2427		$m \cdot \poly(\eps, md/q)$ in place of the stated
2428		$\delta_{\mathrm{combine}}$. The second relation follows from the
2429		analogous argument with the registers swapped.
2430	\end{proof}
