2432	\begin{remark}[The error term in the source proof of
2433		Lemma~\ref{lem:qld-4-13}]
2434		\label{rem:qld-4-13-source-defects}
2435		The statement of Lemma~\ref{lem:qld-4-13} retains the source error
2436		form $\delta_{\mathrm{combine}} = \poly(m^2\eps, md/q)$, which
2437		remains unproved. The source proof in \cite{Ji2020MIPStar} asserts
2438		two different bounds for the quantity
2439		\eqref{eq:qld-combined-lines-consistency}: the bound
2440		$O(m(\eps^{1/4} + \delta_P^{1/4} + \delta_Q^{1/4} +
2441		\delta_{\mathrm{Line}}^{1/2}))$, obtained by chaining the three
2442		claims (Lemmas~\ref{lem:claim-17-1}--\ref{lem:claim-17-3}), and the
2443		bound $O(m^2 \delta_P)$, whose derivation decomposes
2444		\eqref{eq:qld-combined-lines-consistency} into
2445		restricted-distribution terms bounded by
2446		\eqref{eq:qld-xz-lines-restricted}. The second derivation requires a
2447		joint product law for the pair $((\ell_X, x), (\ell_Z, z))$ that
2448		Property~2 of Lemma~\ref{lem:qld-sublines} does not provide, and
2449		neither bound is dominated by a function of $m^2\eps$ and $md/q$
2450		alone that vanishes as its arguments vanish. The proof above
2451		therefore follows the first route only and establishes the bound
2452		$m \cdot \poly(\eps, md/q)$, which is the form consumed by
2453		Lemma~\ref{lem:qld-4-7}, whose error function absorbs the prefactor
2454		$m$ into $(md)^a$. The full analysis --- the two routes, the scalings
2455		showing that the claimed form follows from neither, the corrected
2456		deficit assertion in the proof of Lemma~\ref{lem:claim-17-2}, and the
2457		candidate repairs with their open obligations --- is given in
2458		\cite{gap:qpbt_combined-lines-error-term}.
2459	\end{remark}
