3619	\section{Scalar error estimates}
3620	
3621	The following formalization-only auxiliary statements concern real
3622	functions and numerical parameters, independently of the standing strategy
3623	assumptions of this chapter. They isolate calculations supporting
3624	Lemmas~\ref{lem:qld-xz-lines}, \ref{lem:qld-4-13}, and \ref{lem:qld-4-7}
3625	in \cite{Ji2020MIPStar}; they assert no measurement construction.
3626	Here $p(x)=\poly(x)$ means that $p:\R\to\R$ satisfies
3627	$0\le p(x)\le A x^r$ for all $x\ge0$, for some $A\ge1$ and $r>0$.
3628	Similarly, $f(x,y)=\poly(x,y)$ means
3629	$0\le f(x,y)\le B(x^s+y^t)$ for all $x,y\ge0$, for some $B\ge1$ and
3630	$s,t>0$. These are the corrected error conventions of
3631	\cite{gap:qpbt_polynomial-error-square-root,gap:qpbt_pasting-product-error}.
3632	The functions are defined on all real arguments; these bounds concern their
3633	nonnegative domains.
