573		Expanding one Fourier coefficient at a time through the inversion formula
574		of Lemma~\ref{lem:boolean-fourier-transform} and collapsing the inner
575		character sum with Lemma~\ref{lem:boolean-characters} gives the cubic
576		identity; multiplying it by $\rho$, taking the trace and passing to real
577		parts gives the correlation identity, and the same expansion applied to
578		$\sum_u \widehat{O}^u \, B^u$ gives the overlap identity. Positivity of
579		$B^u$ holds because $\widehat{O}^u$ is Hermitian, so that
580		$B^u = (\widehat{O}^u)^\dagger \widehat{O}^u$, and completeness is the
581		identity $\sum_u (\widehat{O}^u)^2 = \Id$ of
582		Lemma~\ref{lem:boolean-fourier-transform}. The final inequality
583		substitutes the correlation hypothesis into the overlap identity.
584	\end{proof}
